# Architecture Rules

Use a feature-first architecture.

Recommended structure:

lib/
  core/
    constants/
    errors/
    extensions/
    formatters/
    theme/
    utils/
    widgets/
  features/
    transactions/
      domain/
      data/
      application/
      presentation/
    categories/
      domain/
      data/
      application/
      presentation/
    budgets/
      domain/
      data/
      application/
      presentation/
    reports/
      domain/
      data/
      application/
      presentation/
    settings/
      domain/
      data/
      application/
      presentation/

Layer rules:
- presentation: widgets, screens, UI state only.
- application: use cases, controllers, providers, orchestration logic.
- domain: entities, value objects, repository interfaces, pure business rules.
- data: DTOs, local database models, repository implementations, data sources.

Do not:
- Put business logic directly inside Widgets.
- Let UI call database/storage directly.
- Mix unrelated features in the same file.
- Create overly generic abstractions too early.

Prefer:
- Small, focused files.
- Clear naming.
- Repository pattern for data access.
- Pure functions for calculations.
- Feature-level separation.
